  "body": "## What changed\n\nA post script for Mach3 Mill (3-axis).\n\n- `assets/posts/mach3.cps` (new). Derived from our `grblhal.cps`. Mach3 differences:\n  - Tool change: Z goes up, then `T<n> M6` on its own line, then `G43 H<n>`. Mach3 runs the user's M6Start / M6End macros at M6; the post cannot know what they do, so it lifts Z first.\n  - Canned cycles G73, G81, G82, G83, G85, G86, G89 with G98. P on G82, G86 and G89. A dwell on G73, G83 or G85 is refused by name (these cycles have no P word).\n  - Option `dwellInMilliseconds` (off by default): P in milliseconds, for a Mach3 with \"G04 Dwell param in ms\" on in General Config. Off writes seconds.\n  - G91.1 in the header, so arc centres never depend on Mach3's IJ-mode setting.\n  - G41/G42 control compensation, G84 tapping and probing are refused by name.\n  - `axisInversion = true`: a flipped WCS axis or an inverted machine axis posts the mirrored program with its note.\n- `crates/app/src/posting_files.rs`: the post \"Mach3\" after Mach4 (before Heidenhain Klartext), and its embedded copy. The registry now has 21 shipped posts.\n- No new machine. A Mach3 user picks an existing 3-axis machine, for example \"VMC 3-axis\".\n\n## Readings\n\n- `drill_peck.nc`: `T4 M6`, `G43 H4`, then `G98`, `G73 X20 Y10 Z-24 R0 Q18 F60`, `G80`.\n- Header: `G21 G17 G90 G91.1 G94 G40 G49 G80`.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `crates/post/tests/script_mach3.rs` (new): `post_suite!(\"mach3.cps\")` with its recorded goldens.\n- `mach3` added to the shared post tables: `conformance` (with refused cases and the synth stream), `post_spindle_rule_all`, `end_units`, `declared_options`, `comment_escape` (21 shipped posts), `comp`, `control_comp`, `wear_comp`, `after_op`, `fanuc_post`, `bore_cycle` (`SECONDS`: G86 with P in seconds), `dwell_cycles_modal_p` (P0.5 / P0.75), `g73_g85_dwell_linuxcnc` and `wcs_flip_dialects`.\n- App goldens: `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/mach3/*` and `synth_mach3.nc`, written with `WRITE_GOLDEN=1`.\n\n## Gate\n\nThe old red step of the first gate run is not a part of this PR any more. The refresh below ran the named test binaries on head 783b33f6f, and each one is green. A gate-runner runs the rest of the quick plan on the same tree.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No reading on a real Mach3 control and no air cut.\n- That Mach3 accepts G91.1 and P on G86 is from the \"Using Mach3Mill\" word list only, not tested on a control.\n- The `dwellInMilliseconds` option is checked in the goldens only with its default (off).\n\n## Decision\n\n`docs/decisions/2482-mach3-post.md`.\n\n## Refresh by the maintainers\n\nThe maintainer decided that we do the review fixes on this branch. We pushed these commits (a plain fast-forward push, no force-push):\n\n- `2eb78f738` Merge of `origin/main` (22 commits). The merge was clean.\n- `8b7c96079` test(post): make the two stale Mach3 conformance goldens again.\n  - Main changed the slot and the zigzag pocket generators.\n  - `WRITE_GOLDEN=1` changed only `golden/nc/mach3/pocket_zigzag_plate_with_island.nc` and `golden/nc/mach3/slot_wide_channel_rows.nc`.\n  - The tool motion is the same as in the `grblhal` goldens of the same parts: 266 of 266 moves and 27 of 27 moves.\n  - The tool motion is the same as in the `mach4` goldens, but Mach3 has one more `G0 X.. Y..` line at the current Z (the first-traverse law). That line does not move the tool to a different position.\n- `d84792b15` fix(app): list Mach3 with the mill posts, before Heidenhain Klartext. Main added Klartext after the mill posts. After the merge, Mach3 came after Klartext in `BUILTINS`, so two `conformance` tests failed. The names do not change.\n- `ccfe4199e` fix(post): refuse a G73 or G85 dwell in the Mach3 post by name.\n  - Before this change, a PECK or REAM dwell above 0 posted with no P word and no message.\n  - \"Using Mach3Mill\" (release 1.84) gives no P word for these cycles: 10.7.22 `G73 X~ Y~ Z~ A~ B~ C~ R~ L~ Q~` and 10.7.24.6 `G85 X~ Y~ Z~ A~ B~ C~ R~ L~`.\n  - The refusal has the same form as in `grblhal.cps`.\n  - `mach3_refuses_g73_dwell` and `mach3_refuses_g85_dwell` were red before the change and are green after it.\n- `783b33f6f` fix(post): set axisInversion in the Mach3 post and note a WcsFlip.\n  - The script has the same form as `grblhal.cps`: the flag, the inverted-axis header notes, and the `WCS .. FLIPPED - PROGRAM MIRRORED` note.\n  - `mach3` is in the `wcs_flip_dialects` table, with the new golden `crates/post/tests/golden/wcs_flip/mach3_x.nc`.\n  - An upright machine posts the same bytes as before: the Mach3 conformance goldens did not change.\n\nTests on head 783b33f6f (debug, each binary alone):\n\n- `camcraft-post`: `script_mach3` 11, `comment_escape` 4, `comp` 9, `fanuc_post` 12, `end_units` 3, `declared_options` 3, `bore_cycle` 9, `dwell_cycles_modal_p` 5, `g73_g85_dwell_linuxcnc` 9, `wcs_flip_dialects` 9. All pass.\n- `camcraft-app`: `conformance` 7, `after_op` 10, `control_comp` 5, `wear_comp` 5, `post_spindle_rule_all` 5, `machine_library` 16, `mcp_machine_post` 4, `shipped_from_disk` 3, `posting_rotaries_first` 2, `folder_lists` 2. All pass.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Not run yet: the remaining steps of the quick plan and the `app heavy` lanes (`cargo xtask gate heavy --base origin/main`). A gate-runner runs them.\n\nChangelog: New post \"Mach3\": T M6 + G43 H tool change, canned drill cycles with G98, dwell in seconds or milliseconds as a post option; G41/G42, tapping and probing refused.\n\nFixes #2482\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
